00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:28.080
very aligned and in sync so the light is very&nbsp;
energetic and focused into a tiny area it's also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:33.360
one color the light is a particular wavelength&nbsp;
having just the one color of light means that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:38.800
you can target specific things in the skin with&nbsp;
minimal impact on everything else in the skin

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:43.680
so you shoot light into the skin with a laser and&nbsp;
then something in the skin will absorb the light&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:48.240
and when stuff absorbs light it converts&nbsp;
it to other forms of energy like heat

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:51.600
if you put a black thing and a white thing&nbsp;
in the sun the black thing heats up more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:56.800
because black dye absorbs more light energy and&nbsp;
turns it into more heat different things absorb&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:01.440
different wavelengths of light so if you shoot&nbsp;
a particular wavelength of light into the skin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:06.400
a particular colour of light that melanin pigment&nbsp;
absorbs but other things don't really then that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:12.320
means the melanin pigment gets blasted but other&nbsp;
things in your skin don't they have minimal damage

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:16.640
and most lasers work pretty much like&nbsp;
different colored things in the sun&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:20.720
the melanin heats up while the&nbsp;
rest of your skin stays mostly cool

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:24.560
this is called selective&nbsp;
photothermolysis you can select&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:30.480
one thing and use light to heat it up until&nbsp;
it breaks the thing that absorbs the light&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:34.480
the thing in your skin that the laser&nbsp;
is targeting is called the chromophore

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:39.120
apart from melanin the other chromophores in the&nbsp;
skin that lasers usually target are haemoglobin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:44.560
the red chemical in red blood cells and water&nbsp;
so to remove brown pigment patches lasers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:49.840
target melanin to remove red things like broken&nbsp;
capillaries the lasers are targeting haemoglobin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:53.920
skin has a lot of water in it so&nbsp;
the lasers that target water cause&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:58.480
controlled damage to the skin in general&nbsp;
so that hopefully gets the skin to repair&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:03.200
itself in a good way like with more&nbsp;
collagen in a rejuvenating treatment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:08.320
or to smooth out the surface and reduce fine&nbsp;
lines and scars which is called laser resurfacing

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:12.080
different wavelengths also travel&nbsp;
different distances into the skin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:17.200
longer wavelengths get deeper into the skin so&nbsp;
longer wavelengths are used in laser hair removal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:20.960
they can get down deep enough to heat&nbsp;
up and kill cells in the hair root which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:25.200
is all the way down here in the dermis for&nbsp;
